# Layering Rules

Framework-agnostic placement rules. Stack-specific folders live in `backend.mdc` / `frontend.mdc`; **this file wins on "where does this concern belong?"**.

## Package graph (non-negotiable)

```text
apps/web ──► packages/shared          # pure Zod / types; no @elynd/db
apps/api ──► packages/shared
apps/api ──► packages/db              # tables + drizzle-zod
@elynd/shared                         # NO @elynd/db
@elynd/db                             # NO @elynd/shared (unless a concrete need appears)
```

| Rule | Forbidden |
| ---- | --------- |
| One-way deps only | `apps/web` ↔ `apps/api` direct imports; **`shared → db`** |
| Shared packages stay lean | Business workflows inside `@elynd/db` / `@elynd/shared` |
| Schema ownership | Tables/columns/relations defined outside `packages/db` |
| UI ↔ API mix | One file containing both HTTP-server and UI-render concerns |

**Type flow**: `packages/db` and `packages/shared` are siblings; apps compose them. Do not redefine core domain types inside an app if they belong upstream. App-local UI/view types and API-only HTTP DTOs are fine when they are not a shared cross-app contract.

**drizzle-zod composition** belongs in `apps/api` (or stays inside `@elynd/db`). Never import `@elynd/db` from `@elynd/shared`.

Root tooling (not packages): `tsconfig.base.json`, `prettier.config.js`, `eslint.config.mjs`. Nest/Next options stay in each app.

## Concern → layer

| Concern | Lives in | Must not |
| ------- | -------- | -------- |
| Business workflow / domain rules | Feature modules (`apps/api` feature folders, `apps/web/features/**`) | Generic `lib/`, shared config packages |
| Technical capability (crypto, HTTP client, clock, id) | Tech `lib/` / `common/` with **zero** domain knowledge | Import feature modules |
| Transport cross-cutting (auth guard, validation pipe, filters) | API `common/` (or web route guards) | Embed domain workflows |
| Shared Zod / DTO contracts used by **2+** apps | `@elynd/shared` | Duplicate schemas in each app; ORM / drizzle-zod imports |
| API-only HTTP DTOs composed from drizzle-zod | `apps/api` feature schemas | `@elynd/shared` |
| Persistence schema | `@elynd/db` only | Ad-hoc table defs in apps |
| Server/remote state | Query/data layer (not UI store) | Zustand/local store as source of truth for API data |
| Client UI state (modals, theme, ephemeral flags) | UI store | Secrets, tokens-as-business-db, server lists |
| Design-system atoms | `components/ui/**` | Feature business rules |

## Dependency direction inside an app

```text
routes/pages/controllers → application/feature services → tech lib/common → external I/O
```

- **Never** upward imports (lib must not import features).
- **Never** add a layer (repository, use-case, manager, facade) without a concrete pain the current structure cannot absorb.
- Prefer a function call over a new architectural tier.

## Constants and magic values

- Literal used in **2+** modules → named constant in the owning package’s constants (or `@elynd/shared` if cross-app).
- One-off literal → local to the file; do not pre-create unused constants.
- Prefer `as const` objects over TypeScript `enum`.

## Anti-patterns (layering)

- Catch-all `utils/` / `helpers/` that mix unrelated domains
- “Shared” module created for a single consumer
- Copying the same Zod schema into web and API instead of `@elynd/shared`
- Importing `@elynd/db` from `@elynd/shared`
- Putting workflow orchestration into DB schema files or UI primitives
- Storing server-derived lists in client UI stores
- Cross-importing feature modules when the shared bit is actually a tech capability → move to tech lib instead
